    "finalMessage": "The film is built and runs: the book opens, the castle, jungle, port and snowy peaks pop up in turn with the camera moving between them, and the book closes by 29.4 s so the loop restarts on the closed book.\n\nI checked it in headless Chrome at 1280\u00d7720: 12 frozen frames across the film (including `?t=0` and `?t=30`) plus one autoplay run, all with zero console messages. I only reviewed still frames, so the motion itself (page turns, fold timing, camera path between shots) has not been watched in real time. The screenshots were taken over `file://` with a Chrome flag, not through a static server.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` \u2014 entry point, import map for Three.js 0.170.0 from jsDelivr\n- `src/main.js` \u2014 renderer, lights, table, render loop, `?t=` handling\n- `src/timeline.js` \u2014 the 30-second schedule (cover, page turns, each world's fold amount)\n- `src/camera.js` \u2014 camera keyframes and interpolation\n- `src/paper.js` \u2014 shared paper-card helpers and the pop-up fold mechanism\n- `src/book.js` \u2014 covers, page blocks, turning leaves\n- `src/world-castle.js`\n- `src/world-jungle.js`\n- `src/world-port.js`\n- `src/world-mountains.js`\n\n## How to view\n\nFrom this folder, run any static server, for example:\n\n```\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/` to play the film, or `http://localhost:8000/index.html?t=12.5` to freeze at a given second.\n\n## Things to know\n\n- **Leftover folder:** `.shots/` holds my verification screenshots and Chrome logs. I couldn't delete it (permission denied); remove it with `rm -rf .shots`.\n- **Nothing is committed.** `git status` printed nothing even with the new files present, so this folder appears to be git-ignored.\n- **Jungle worker ran out of steps:** `src/world-jungle.js` was left by a worker that stopped while still adding detail. It passes the syntax check and renders correctly in the screenshots, but it never had a clean \"done\" report."
  },
